                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99f7ff5c-63b6-3d19-8064-c0ce8c6b2dfb",
                                        "entry_id": "b4ff4228-bb4a-33ba-acc5-372b98416121",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of decision making."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "139a9196-bfea-47be-ba61-0ada81a74078",
                                                "sense_id": "99f7ff5c-63b6-3d19-8064-c0ce8c6b2dfb",
                                                "text": "But what if Google's biggest problem isn't a lack of flexibility or the speed of its decision-making, but a fundamental cultural inability to create new lines of business that can keep the company growing? What if it's just a gargantuan one-trick pony?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99141a3a-73fd-4521-b17b-9e5febfb5dda",
                                                "sense_id": "99f7ff5c-63b6-3d19-8064-c0ce8c6b2dfb",
                                                "text": "The projects, which are due to start in November, are: [...] Rail performance modelling for strategic decision-making - [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e58be530-b9af-4bf6-b15c-0b1d3669660f",
                                                "sense_id": "99f7ff5c-63b6-3d19-8064-c0ce8c6b2dfb",
                                                "text": "Transport Minister Mulley, with just six months left in office before Harold Wilson's Labour government was toppled by Edward Heath's Conservatives, was hamstrung by inefficient working practices - although thankfully for him he did not have to answer to 2020-style media questioning over why slow decision-making allowed costs to escalate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
